title: The cost of the inner loop
prompt: In `daily_temperatures`, a single day can pop many waiting days at once. Why doesn't that make the function O(n²)?
* Each day is pushed once and popped at most once, so all the pops over the whole run add up to at most n :: Right. A day that pops a lot uses up waiting days that can't be popped again.
- The `while` loop never pops more than one day at a time :: It can pop many: a very warm day pops every colder day waiting.
