title: Indexes, not values
prompt: Why does `daily_temperatures` push indexes onto its stack instead of temperatures?
* An index gives both where to write the answer and how far apart the two days are, and the temperature can still be read as `temps[j]` :: Right. A temperature alone loses the day it belongs to.
